  "body": "   Falling bodies . Using the base instead of the base 2, modify the solution to the initial value problem that appears in . Show that the modified expression is still a solution.   If an object that falls against air resistance is meters above the ground after seconds, and it started meters above the ground, then it is the solution of the initial value problem where is the velocity function from the previous exercise. Find a formula for using the exponential function with base . (Compare this formula with the one in .)   Suppose the coefficient of air resistance is 0.2 per second. If a body is held motionless 200 meters above the ground, and then released, how far will it fall in 1 second? In 2 seconds? Use your formula from part (b). Compare these values with those you obtained in .   "
